# --- third-party runtime binaries (fetched, NOT vendored) ---
# wintun.dll is proprietary ((c) WireGuard LLC, "licensed, not sold" — see its
# own LICENSE.txt) and must never land in this AGPL repo. It is a Windows-client
# runtime dependency fetched from wintun.net and staged here at build/package
# time. See clients/windows/README.md ("wintun runtime dependency").
/clients/windows/wintun/

# --- third-party datasets (fetched, NOT vendored) ---
# The GeoLite2 Country database the coordinator derives node countries from
# (issue #136, ADR-0042). It is a licensed MaxMind dataset under its own terms,
# not ours to redistribute, and it is bulk data besides — so it is staged out of
# band and refreshed on MaxMind's cadence, never committed. See docs/RUNNING.md
# ("GeoIP country database").
/geoip/
GeoLite2-Country-*.csv
GeoLite2-Country-*.mmdb
GeoLite2-Country-CSV_*/

# --- go ---
/vendor/

# --- editor / OS ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# --- local scratch notes at the repo root (NEVER commit) ---
# The repo root is where per-checkout notes, task briefs and tooling scratch
# files get dropped, and several such conventions put them in markdown with a
# fixed name. Committing one leaks local working context into a public repo, so
# the root is closed by default and this repo's own documents are allowlisted
# below. This is deliberately a denylist-by-default: it also catches whatever
# the next convention happens to be called, which naming individual files
# cannot. Adding a genuinely new root-level document means adding it here —
# `git add` fails loudly on an ignored path, so it cannot pass unnoticed.
/*.md
!/README.md
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/CONVENTIONS.md
!/SECURITY.md
